    "done_when": "First, packages/imas-alambic/install/imasdb.sh /home/SharedFolder/d240044/IMASDB is rerun at the base so the facility tool carries the on-demand fetch and its launcher exports IMAS_ALAMBIC_EDDB_HOST=local; its gate log names that revision and ends with EXIT=0. Then on intr26-2, through ssh jt-60sa with no IMAS_ALAMBIC_* variable set and under nice -n 19, /usr/bin/time -v /home/SharedFolder/d240044/IMASDB/bin/imas-alambic write 101154 exits 0, fetching E101154 through the local EDDB transport into the account cache and writing /home/SharedFolder/d240044/IMASDB/ids/101154_0.nc; the wall time and maximum resident set size from time -v are recorded. Here, uv run --no-sync imas-alambic write 101154 --machine jt-60sa --maps /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/maps --out a scratch directory under the run directory writes the comparison file from the same bundle version 2026.10.07, leaving /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/ids untouched. The server file is copied back with scp into the run directory, and for every IDS in it imas.util.idsdiffgen(server_ids, here_ids) yields no difference; the IDS set equals the E101154 phase description set. The server file mode grants others r--. Nothing on the server is written outside IMASDB and the account cache ~/.cache/imas-alambic. Every command and its output is captured once to logs under the run directory.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
